 service. We are an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer, and in keeping with this commitment, we welcome all to apply, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Job Description: Budget title:  Instructional Support Associate (SL-2) Salary:  Commensurate with Experience (part-time, 65% FTE) Binghamton University, a NCAA Division I institution and member of the America East Conference, is seeking a Director of Operations/Assistant Women's Basketball Coach.  The Director of Operations/Assistant Women's Basketball Coach provides administrative support for all aspects of the women's basketball program. This position assists the Head Coach with daily basketball operations, player development, practice planning, travel coordination, budgeting, compliance, and student-athlete development. The successful candidate will foster a culture of academic excellence, competitive success, and personal growth while ensuring compliance with institutional, conference, and NCAA regulations. Requirements: Bachelor's degree (or higher) Preferred: Master's degree Minimum of 1 year experience at the Division 1 intercollegiate athletics level Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that Binghamton University is not an E-Verify employer. Additional Information: Special Notes: This position is considered a Campus Security Authority for purposes of Clery Act compliance Offers of employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a pre-employment background check and verification of degree(s) and credentials Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus. Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history,