    "https://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204087": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Russian Studies",
      "description": "Binghamton University\nJob Posting: Assistant or Associate Professor of Russian Studies Binghamton University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant or Associate Professor of Russian Studies Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant or Associate Professor of Russian Studies Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Department of German and Russian Studies, Harpur College Locations: Binghamton, NY Posted: Aug 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 7031 Position ID: 204087 Share About Binghamton University: Binghamton University is a premier public R1 research institution in the State University of New York (SUNY) system that unites more than 130 broadly interdisciplinary educational programs with some of the most vibrant research in the nation. Our unique character - shaped by our mission, outstanding academics, facilities, and community life - promotes extraordinary student success, research, and service; Binghamton University is where our students, faculty and staff thrive. Working at Binghamton University is more than about having a great job - it is about having the opportunity to flourish in an exciting, engaging environment. Our faculty and staff appreciate Binghamton's collegial and inclusive culture and its commitment to excellence, education, innovation, and civic engagement. Our diverse campus community contributes to our success. Binghamton merges rigorous academics, distinguished faculty who value cutting-edge, and community-engaged research, teaching and service, exceptional staff, and ultramodern facilities to engage and challenge its 18,000+ students. Our high-achieving student body represents diverse experiences from first-generation college-goers to international students. Beyond their talent, these classmates share a desire to shape the future through technology, insight, intellectual exploration, and community service. Job Description: The Department of German and Russian Studies at Binghamton University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor, beginning August 2027. The research specialization for this position is open, and candidates specializing in any aspect of Russian Studies from Early Slavic to the present are encouraged to apply. We are particularly interested in candidates with research trajectories in areas including Russian-Jewish Literature and Culture, the Literatures and Cultures of Russian-speaking Diasporas, and/or Ethnically Diverse Russian-speaking Cultures; as well as 21st-century Russian-language Literature and/or Media Studies, Gender and Sexuality Studies, Environmental Humanities, and other research areas that would complement existing departmental and interdisciplinary research communities at Binghamton. The successful applicant will successfully teach the Russian language and core courses in Russian-language culture, be able to offer new undergraduate courses within their research area, and imaginatively contribute to undergraduate outreach, curricular development, and program growth. We enthusiastically invite applications from those at the ABD level as well as advanced Assistant or early Associate rank. Applicants at the Associate level should further demonstrate capacity for program leadership. The successful candidate will be part of the core faculty of the Russian Program, home to the only formalized undergraduate Russian Major in the State University of New York, the largest public university system in the state. Opportunities for growth include participation in the interdisciplinary Russian, East European, and Eurasian Studies Program, teaching in the East European Studies Minor, and collaborating with campus colleagues teaching in 17 language programs, the most languages taught at any single campus in the SUNY system. They will also join a university-wide intellectual cohort of recent strategic hires in a broad range of emerging fields in the humanities, among which Russian-speaking diasporas broadly understood would be of great interest. This position is represented by UUP, the largest higher education union in the country, which has recently secured a five-year contract with historic gains, including very strong annual raises and job protections around AI. We are especially interested in applicants who view research, teaching, program building, and outreach as areas to promote diversity and perspectives that are underrepresented in higher education. Binghamton University is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. Requirements: Required Qualifications 1.    PhD in Slavic Languages and Literatures or related field by August 16, 2027 2.    Native or near-native proficiency in English and Russian 3.    Evidence of a strong research agenda 4.    Experience teaching Russian language at the college level Preferred Qualifications 1.    Evidence of research productivity in Russian-Jewish Literature and Culture, the Literatures and Cultures of Russian-speaking Diasporas, Ethnically-diverse Russian-speaking Cultures, or a related sub-field. Please be advised that H1B visa sponsorship may not be available for this position. Additional Information: Binghamton University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, please contact the ADA Coordinator by completing the following Request Form . The State University of New York is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. It is the policy of Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the basis of age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military service member status, marital status, domestic violence victim status, genetic predisposition or carrier status, or arrest and/or criminal conviction record unless based upon a bona fide occupational qualification or other exception. As required by title IX and its implementing regulations, Binghamton University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the educational programs and activities which it operates. This requirement extends to employment and admission. Inquiries about sex discrimination may be directed to the University Title IX Coordinator or directly to the Office of Civil Rights (OCR). Contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and OCR, as well as the University's complete Non-Discrimination Notice may be found here. Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation. If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor's Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov. Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus effective August 1, 2017. Offers of employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a pre-employment background check and verification of degree(s) and credentials. Application Instructions: All applicants must apply via Interview Exchange: http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204087 Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the vacancy is filled. Please submit: Cover letter, CV, Research statement, Statement of teaching philosophy, and Names and email addresses of three references. Letters of recommendation and supplementary materials will be requested for candidates whose applications advance in the selection process. The position will remain open until filled. Applications received by October 15 will receive priority consideration. We anticipate that first-round interviews will be conducted over Zoom in mid-December, with campus visits taking place early in the spring semester. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Binghamton University State University of New York 4400 Vestal Parkway East, Binghamton, NY 13902"
    },
    "https://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203674": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Binghamton University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Binghamton University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Clinical Psychology Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Department of Psychology, Harpur College Locations: Binghamton, NY Posted: Aug 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 559 Position ID: 203674 Share About Binghamton University: Binghamton University is a premier public R1 research institution in the State University of New York (SUNY) system that unites more than 130 broadly interdisciplinary educational programs with some of the most vibrant research in the nation. Our unique character - shaped by our mission, outstanding academics, facilities, and community life - promotes extraordinary student success, research, and service; Binghamton University is where our students, faculty and staff thrive. Working at Binghamton University is more than about having a great job - it is about having the opportunity to flourish in an exciting, engaging environment. Our faculty and staff appreciate Binghamton's collegial and inclusive culture and its commitment to excellence, education, innovation, and civic engagement. Our diverse campus community contributes to our success. Binghamton merges rigorous academics, distinguished faculty who value cutting-edge, and community-engaged research, teaching and service, exceptional staff, and ultramodern facilities to engage and challenge its 18,000+ students. Our high-achieving student body represents diverse experiences from first-generation college-goers to international students. Beyond their talent, these classmates share a desire to shape the future through technology, insight, intellectual exploration, and community service. Job Description: The Department of Psychology at Binghamton University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in the Clinical Science Ph.D. Program, with a research focus on schizophrenia and other severe mental illnesses (SMI). Our program holds dual accreditation from PCSAS and the APA Commission on Accreditation and is a member of the Academy of Psychological Clinical Science. We seek a clinical scientist whose research advances mechanistic understanding of psychotic and SMI, including etiology, assessment development, and intervention research. Methodological approach is open and may include cognitive, neural, psychophysiological, computational, social, or psychosocial approaches. Candidates are especially encouraged to apply if their methods take advantage of the Brain and Body Imaging Research Center (BBIRC), a 3T Siemens MAGNETOM Prisma facility opened in 2023 through partnership with United Health Services, or who would build collaborations with the Greater Binghamton Health Center (GBHC) and the OnTrackNY early-psychosis program. The Department values scholarship that bridges scientific rigor with community impact. The Psychology Department consists of 48 faculty members in three doctoral programs (Behavioral Neuroscience, Clinical Science, and Cognitive and Brain Sciences), as well as eight teaching faculty offering additional expertise in developmental, school, forensic, and social psychology. We recognize that excellence is often informed by varied life experiences. We therefore welcome applicants with non-traditional career trajectories or significant professional experience outside of academia. The Department prizes collegiality at all ranks, is family-friendly, and there is a pre-school on campus. Additional information about the Department is available at https://www.binghamton.edu/psychology/ . Binghamton University is dedicated to advancing equity and inclusion, and in particular to the goal of building a diverse and inclusive teaching, research, and working environment, including a diverse faculty. Evidence of a commitment to advancing equity and inclusion through research, teaching, and/or service will be valued. Potential applicants who share this goal, especially members of groups historically underrepresented in the field and those from non-traditional backgrounds, women, and persons with disabilities, are strongly encouraged to apply. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology or a related discipline by August 16, 2027. An active program of research as demonstrated by a history of peer-reviewed publications and/or extramural funding. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching undergraduate or graduate courses New York State licensure eligibility Please be advised that H1B visa sponsorship may not be available for this position. Additional Information: Binghamton University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, please contact the ADA Coordinator by completing the following Request Form . The State University of New York is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. It is the policy of Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the basis of age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military service member status, marital status, domestic violence victim status, genetic predisposition or carrier status, or arrest and/or criminal conviction record unless based upon a bona fide occupational qualification or other exception. As required by title IX and its implementing regulations, Binghamton University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the educational programs and activities which it operates. This requirement extends to employment and admission. Inquiries about sex discrimination may be directed to the University Title IX Coordinator or directly to the Office of Civil Rights (OCR). Contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and OCR, as well as the University's complete Non-Discrimination Notice may be found here. Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation. If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor's Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov. Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus effective August 1, 2017. Offers of employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a pre-employment background check and verification of degree(s) and credentials. Application Instructions: To apply, submit the following via Interview Exchange: http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203674 Curriculum vitae; Cover letter describing your area of expertise, experience, and interest in the position; Research statement; Teaching statement; Contact information for three references from whom we might request confidential letters of recommendation. Complete applications received by October 1, 2026 will receive full consideration. The position will remain open until filled. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Binghamton University State University of New York 4400 Vestal Parkway East, Binghamton, NY 13902"
    },
    "https://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203309": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Binghamton University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Accounting Binghamton University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Accounting Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Accounting Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Management Locations: Binghamton, NY Posted: Aug 4, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 2100 Position ID: 203309 Share About Binghamton University: Binghamton University is a premier public R1 research institution in the State University of New York (SUNY) system that unites more than 130 broadly interdisciplinary educational programs with some of the most vibrant research in the nation. Our unique character - shaped by our mission, outstanding academics, facilities, and community life - promotes extraordinary student success, research, and service; Binghamton University is where our students, faculty and staff thrive. Working at Binghamton University is more than about having a great job - it is about having the opportunity to flourish in an exciting, engaging environment. Our faculty and staff appreciate Binghamton's collegial and inclusive culture and its commitment to excellence, education, innovation, and civic engagement. Our diverse campus community contributes to our success. Binghamton merges rigorous academics, distinguished faculty who value cutting-edge, and community-engaged research, teaching and service, exceptional staff, and ultramodern facilities to engage and challenge its 18,000+ students. Our high-achieving student body represents diverse experiences from first-generation college-goers to international students. Beyond their talent, these classmates share a desire to shape the future through technology, insight, intellectual exploration, and community service. Job Description: About Us The School of Management (SOM) holds separate AACSB accreditations in Business and Accounting and is nationally recognized for its success in developing future business leaders.  SOM is listed as one of the top business schools among fully public institutions by Poets&Quants . The School offers bachelor's, master's, and Ph.D. programs. SOM consistently ranks among the top business schools for our undergraduate and graduate business programs. The Accounting faculty have a consistent record of scholarly achievement.  Recent accounting faculty publications have appeared in Journal of Accounting Research , The Accounting Review , Contemporary Accounting Research , Review of Accounting Studies , Auditing: A Journal of Practice and Theory and Behavioral Research in Accounting . For more information about the School of Management, visit our website: http://www.binghamton.edu/som/ . Job Description: The School of Management (SOM) at Binghamton University (State University of New York at Binghamton) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level in Accounting starting mid-August 2027, subject to budgetary approval. Key Responsibilities: Produce high quality research in top-tier accounting journals.  To support faculty research, SOM provides summer funding for the first three years of service. Deliver required/elective courses in accounting at the undergraduate and/or master's levels.  The standard teaching load is 2+2 per academic year. Contribute to the school, the university, and the professional community by providing appropriate service through involvement in committees, shared governance undertakings, curriculum development and assessment. Actively contribute to the intellectual environment of the area. Requirements: Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Accounting or a closely related field, or will have completed all degree requirements by the academic year obligation start date (August 16, 2027), including securing valid immigration status and work authorization, if applicable. Ability to establish a successful track record of scholarly research.  This can be substantiated by providing copies of applicant's dissertation, publications, and working papers. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience as evidenced by favorable teaching evaluations. The ability and willingness to teach Accounting Information Systems and/or Forensic Accounting. Please be advised that H1B visa sponsorship may not be available for this position. Additional Information: Binghamton University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, please contact the ADA Coordinator by completing the following Request Form . The State University of New York is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. It is the policy of Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the basis of age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military service member status, marital status, domestic violence victim status, genetic predisposition or carrier status, or arrest and/or criminal conviction record unless based upon a bona fide occupational qualification or other exception. As required by title IX and its implementing regulations, Binghamton University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the educational programs and activities which it operates. This requirement extends to employment and admission. Inquiries about sex discrimination may be directed to the University Title IX Coordinator or directly to the Office of Civil Rights (OCR). Contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and OCR, as well as the University's complete Non-Discrimination Notice may be found here. Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation. If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor's Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov. Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus effective August 1, 2017. Offers of employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a pre-employment background check and verification of degree(s) and credentials. Application Instructions: Application materials must be submitted electronically for consideration.  Interested applicants must submit the following documents to the appropriate position listing through Interview Exchange: http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203309 Cover letter; Curriculum Vitae (CV); Job market paper; Research statement; Teaching statement; Contact information for three references.  Reference letters will be requested at a subsequent stage in the recruitment process. You may add additional files/documents after uploading your resume. After you fill out your contact information, you will be directed to the upload page. Please login to check/edit your profile or to upload additional documents: http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/login.jsp. Evaluation of application materials begins immediately and continues until the positions are filled.  Preliminary interviews with candidates will be conducted online via Zoom. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Binghamton University State University of New York 4400 Vestal Parkway East, Binghamton, NY 13902"
    },
    "https://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202743": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Strategy",
      "description": "Binghamton University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Strategy Binghamton University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Strategy Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Strategy Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Management Locations: Binghamton, NY Posted: Jul 17, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 7654 Position ID: 202743 Share About Binghamton University: Binghamton University is a premier public R1 research institution in the State University of New York (SUNY) system that unites more than 130 broadly interdisciplinary educational programs with some of the most vibrant research in the nation. Our unique character - shaped by our mission, outstanding academics, facilities, and community life - promotes extraordinary student success, research, and service; Binghamton University is where our students, faculty and staff thrive. Working at Binghamton University is more than about having a great job - it is about having the opportunity to flourish in an exciting, engaging environment. Our faculty and staff appreciate Binghamton's collegial and inclusive culture and its commitment to excellence, education, innovation, and civic engagement. Our diverse campus community contributes to our success. Binghamton merges rigorous academics, distinguished faculty who value cutting-edge, and community-engaged research, teaching and service, exceptional staff, and ultramodern facilities to engage and challenge its 18,000+ students. Our high-achieving student body represents diverse experiences from first-generation college-goers to international students. Beyond their talent, these classmates share a desire to shape the future through technology, insight, intellectual exploration, and community service. Job Description: The School of Management at Binghamton University (State University of New York at Binghamton) invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level in the area of Strategy starting mid-August 2027, subject to budgetary approval. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. degree or will have completed all degree requirements by the academic year obligation start date (August 16, 2027).  We welcome applications from candidates with backgrounds in Management or other interdisciplinary fields (i.e., sustainability, psychology, etc.).  The school is non-departmentalized, and faculty work with colleagues from a number of management disciplines. The salary and benefits package are competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications.  To support faculty research, SOM provides summer funding for the first three years of service. The start date for the position is August 16, 2027. About Us The School of Management (SOM) holds separate AACSB accreditations in Business and Accounting and is nationally recognized for its success in developing future business leaders. SOM is listed as one of the top business schools among fully public institutions by Poets&Quants . The School offers bachelor's, master's, and Ph.D. programs. SOM consistently ranks among the top business schools for our undergraduate and graduate business programs. Faculty in the School of Management have a strong collegial relationship and regularly collaborate on research topics that integrate micro/macro levels and various disciplines, leverage different methodological perspectives (e.g., qualitative, quantitative and mixed-method approaches), and utilize extant multilevel and other advanced analytical tools. We are seeking a researcher who would complement this orientation with strong methodological and analytical foundations with a willingness to engage in multilevel and interdisciplinary research. Faculty have published in high-quality journals that include:  Academy of Management Journal, Journal of Applied Psychology, Marketing Science, Management Science, Manufacturing and Service Operations Management Journal, Journal of Business Ethics, Journal of Management, Journal of Management Studies, Leadership Quarterly, Organizational Research Methods, Organization Studies, Organization Science, and Personnel Psychology. Additionally, our faculty have received external funding from federal agencies including: Army Research Institute, Department of Defense, Federal Emergency Management Association, and the National Science Foundation. For more information about the School of Management, visit our website: http://www.binghamton.edu/som/ . Key Responsibilities: Produce original and innovative research to be published in top-tier business academic journals. Deliver required/elective courses in strategy at the undergraduate and graduate program levels.  The standard teaching load is 2+2 per academic year. Actively participate in the school's graduate programs and graduate student advising. Contribute to the school, the university, and the professional community by providing appropriate service through involvement in committees, shared governance undertakings, curriculum development and assessment. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in Management or other interdisciplinary fields (i.e., sustainability, psychology, etc.), or have completed all degree requirements (including securing valid immigration status and work authorization, if applicable) by the academic year obligation start date (August 16, 2027). Demonstrated potential to establish a successful track record of scholarly research. This can be substantiated by providing copies of published articles, submitted manuscripts, and work-in-progress papers aimed at publication in top-tier journals. Evidence of a strong and active research agenda focused on strategic management topics (e.g., competitive advantage, corporate strategy, innovation, entrepreneurship, global strategy, or corporate governance). Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated multilevel research skills. Demonstrated innovative teaching capabilities. Demonstrated analytical, quantitative, and data management training directed towards addressing strategic business challenges and improving managerial decision-making. Please be advised that H1B visa sponsorship may not be available for this position. Additional Information: Binghamton University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, please contact the ADA Coordinator by completing the following Request Form . The State University of New York is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. It is the policy of Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the basis of age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military service member status, marital status, domestic violence victim status, genetic predisposition or carrier status, or arrest and/or criminal conviction record unless based upon a bona fide occupational qualification or other exception. As required by title IX and its implementing regulations, Binghamton University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the educational programs and activities which it operates. This requirement extends to employment and admission. Inquiries about sex discrimination may be directed to the University Title IX Coordinator or directly to the Office of Civil Rights (OCR). Contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and OCR, as well as the University's complete Non-Discrimination Notice may be found here. Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation. If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor's Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov. Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus effective August 1, 2017. Offers of employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a pre-employment background check and verification of degree(s) and credentials. Application Instructions: All applicants must apply via Interview Exchange: http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202743 Cover letter; Curriculum Vitae (CV); Research statement; Teaching statement; Contact information for three references.  Reference letters will be requested at a subsequent state in the recruitment process. You may add additional files/documents after uploading your resume.  After you fill out your contact information, you will be directed to the upload page.  Please login to check/edit your profile or to upload additional documents:  http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/login.jsp. Evaluation of application materials begins immediately and continues until the position is filled.  Preliminary interviews with candidates will be conducted online via Zoom. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Binghamton University State University of New York 4400 Vestal Parkway East, Binghamton, NY 13902"
