      "title": "Intro Biology Lab Instructional Support Associate",
      "description": "Binghamton University\nJob Posting: Intro Biology Lab Instructional Support Associate Binghamton University \n\tJob Posting: Intro Biology Lab Instructional Support Associate Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Intro Biology Lab Instructional Support Associate Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Biological Sciences Locations: Binghamton, NY Posted: Sep 4, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 07101 Position ID: 204462 Share About Binghamton University: Binghamton University is a premier public R1 research institution in the State University of New York (SUNY) system that unites more than 130 broadly interdisciplinary educational programs with some of the most vibrant research in the nation. Our unique character - shaped by our mission, outstanding academics, facilities, and community life - promotes extraordinary student success, research, and service; Binghamton University is where our students, faculty and staff thrive. Working at Binghamton University is more than about having a great job - it is about having the opportunity to flourish in an exciting, engaging environment. Our faculty and staff appreciate Binghamton's collegial and inclusive culture and its commitment to excellence, education, innovation and civic engagement. Our diverse campus community contributes to our success. Binghamton merges rigorous academics, distinguished faculty who value cutting-edge, and community-engaged research, teaching and service, exceptional staff, and ultramodern facilities to engage and challenge its 18,000+ students. Our high-achieving student body represents diverse experiences from first-generation college-goers to international students. Beyond their talent, these classmates share a desire to shape the future through technology, insight, intellectual exploration, and community service. We are an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer, and in keeping with this commitment, we welcome all to apply, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Job Description: Budget Title:  Instructional Support Associate (SL-2) Salary:  $54,090 The Department of Biological Sciences at Binghamton University ( http://www.binghamton.edu/biology/ ) is seeking candidates for a full-time position as an Intro Biology Lab Instructional Support Associate for the intro biology laboratory courses, beginning Fall 2026. Duties include but are not limited to: Maintaining Daphnia magna and algae cultures utilized in Intro Biology Lab (Biol 115) Preparing reagents and materials needed in Biol 115 Ordering supplies and equipment for Biol 115 Setting up the laboratory instrumentation used, including setup and breakdown of lab stations Maintaining inventories and monitoring the condition of the equipment used in the introductory lab course and recommending replacement and repairs as needed. Working with teaching assistants to familiarize them with protocols and instrumentation for instructional purposes May be asked to teach a laboratory section of Biol 115 and hold office hours Requirements: Bachelor's degree (or higher) in biology or related field Effective organizational and written/verbal communication skills Ability to stand for prolonged periods of time Ability to push/pull/lift up to 50 lbs Ability working with a diverse group of individuals Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree (or higher) in biology or a related field Work experience at the college level Demonstrated training or experience in biology Laboratory experience Teaching experience Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that Binghamton University is not an E-Verify employer. Additional Information: Offers of employment wi