    "https://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204139": {
      "title": "International Student and Scholar Advisor",
      "description": "Binghamton University\nJob Posting: International Student and Scholar Advisor Binghamton University \n\tJob Posting: International Student and Scholar Advisor Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details International Student and Scholar Advisor Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: International Students & Scholars Services Locations: Binghamton, NY Posted: Aug 31, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 47605 Position ID: 204139 Share About Binghamton University: Binghamton University is a premier public R1 research institution in the State University of New York (SUNY) system that unites more than 130 broadly interdisciplinary educational programs with some of the most vibrant research in the nation. Our unique character - shaped by our mission, outstanding academics, facilities, and community life - promotes extraordinary student success, research, and service; Binghamton University is where our students, faculty and staff thrive. Working at Binghamton University is more than about having a great job - it is about having the opportunity to flourish in an exciting, engaging environment. Our faculty and staff appreciate Binghamton's collegial and inclusive culture and its commitment to excellence, education, innovation and civic engagement. Our diverse campus community contributes to our success. Binghamton merges rigorous academics, distinguished faculty who value cutting-edge, and community-engaged research, teaching and service, exceptional staff, and ultramodern facilities to engage and challenge its 18,000+ students. Our high-achieving student body represents diverse experiences from first-generation college-goers to international students. Beyond their talent, these classmates share a desire to shape the future through technology, insight, intellectual exploration, and community service. We are an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer, and in keeping with this commitment, we welcome all to apply, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Job Description: Budget Title:  Senior Staff Assistant (SL-3) Salary:  $58,000 This position reports to the Associate Director of the Office of International Student and Scholar Services (ISSS) within International Education and Global Affairs (IEGA). The International Student and Scholar Advisor plays a key role in ensuring the university's compliance with federal regulations governing international students, exchange visitors, and visiting scholars. The position requires the application of specialized knowledge of U.S. immigration regulations, as well as university academic policies and procedures. Working in a dynamic and collaborative environment, the advisor serves as an integral member of multiple teams, including immigration and insurance advising, front desk operations, SEVIS management, information technology, ISSS, and IEGA. The advisor will help plan, coordinate, and implement programs and services that support the university community, while partnering with ISSS colleagues and campus stakeholders to advance the mission and strategic goals of the office. The advisor is responsible for maintaining Student and Exchange Visitor Information System (SEVIS) compliance and ensuring the accuracy and integrity of related university systems and records. The successful candidate will serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) and Alternate Responsible Officer (ARO), as authorized by the U.S. Department of Homeland Security and the U.S. Department of State, respectively. In addition, the advisor acts as a liaison between ISSS and university administrative offices, as well as community partners, to support the needs of international students, scholars, and the broader campus community. Duties: Advise international students and scholars through in-person, virtual, telephone, and email consultations on immigration-related matters, university policies, and available resources. Serve as a proactive and collaborative team member, communicating and interpreting departmental immigration policies, procedures, and regulatory requirements. Act as a liaison with state and federal agencies, including but not limited to the Student and Exchange Visitor Program (SEVP), Social Security Administration (SSA), and Department of Motor Vehicles (DMV). Exercise sound professional judgment in making informed and independent determinations regarding eligibility for immigration benefits while balancing regulatory compliance, institutional policy, and customer service considerations. Support and staff programs, events, and initiatives sponsored by ISSS and partner offices across the university. Develop and deliver presentations at orientations, workshops, and informational sessions for students, scholars, campus partners, and professional audiences, both on campus and at conferences, as assigned. Serve on departmental, divisional, and university committees as appropriate and as determined by departmental leadership. Represent ISSS and Binghamton University at professional meetings, conferences, and other engagements within SUNY and in external professional organizations. Collaborate with campus partners to promote international student and scholar success and advance the mission of ISSS and the university. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to exercise discretion, independent judgment, and sound decision-making in complex and evolving situations. Demonstrated ability to learn, interpret, and communicate highly technical information, regulations, and procedures to diverse audiences. Effective organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to maintain accuracy in a compliance-focused environment. Written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to identify goals, develop strategies, and plan and implement programs and activities to achieve desired outcomes. Ability to build and maintain effective working relationships with a diverse range of university and community stakeholders. Proven ability to work effectively under pressure, manage competing priorities, and adapt to frequent interruptions in a fast-paced environment. Requirements: Bachelor's degree Experience navigating and managing complex organizational processes, policies, and procedures Experience working effectively across cultures and with individuals from diverse backgrounds Demonstrated experience providing advising, training, workshops, or presentations Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and Google Workspace applications Note:  In accordance with federal regulations governing Designated School Officials (DSOs) and Alternate Responsible Officers (AROs), candidates must be able to demonstrate U.S. citizenship or lawful permanent resident status. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree Professional experience advising international students and scholars on federal immigration related requirements Proficiency with SEVIS and/or SUNAPSIS systems Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that Binghamton University is not an E-Verify employer. Additional Information: Offers of employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a pre-employment background check and verification of degree(s) and credentials Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus. Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation.  If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor's Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov Payroll information can be found on our website https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/payroll/ Cover letters may be addressed \"To the Search Committee.\" Postings active on the website, accept applications until closure. For information on the Dual Career Program, please visit: https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/prospective/dual-career/index.html Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer The State University of New York is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer.  It is the policy of Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the basis of age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military service member status, marital status, domestic violence victim status, genetic predisposition or carrier status, or arrest and/or criminal conviction record unless based upon a bona fide occupational qualification or other exception. As required by Title IX and its implementing regulations Binghamton University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the educational programs and activities which it operates.  This requirement extends to employment and admission.  Inquiries about sex discrimination may be directed to the University Title IX Coordinator or directly to the Office of Civil Rights (OCR).  Contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and OCR, as well as the University's complete Non-Discrimination Notice may be found here . Binghamton University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, contact the ADA Coordinator by completing the Reasonable Accommodation Request Form . Application Instructions: All applicants must apply via Interview Exchange: http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=204139 Deadline for Internal Applicants:  September 15, 2026 Deadline for External Applicants:  Open until filled Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the vacancy is filled. Please submit: Resume, Cover letter, and Contact information for three professional references You may add additional files/documents after uploading your resume. After you fill out your contact information, you will be directed to the upload page. Please login to check/edit your profile or to upload additional documents: http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/login.jsp . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Binghamton University State University of New York 4400 Vestal Parkway East, Binghamton, NY 13902"
