    "https://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203486": {
      "title": "PRODiG+ Fellow: Libraries' Postdoctoral Associate in Info Analytics, Assessment, and User Experience",
      "description": "Binghamton University\nJob Posting: PRODiG+ Fellow: Libraries' Postdoctoral Associate in Info Analytics, Assessment, and User Experience Binghamton University \n\tJob Posting: PRODiG+ Fellow: Libraries' Postdoctoral Associate in Info Analytics, Assessment, and User Experience Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details PRODiG+ Fellow: Libraries' Postdoctoral Associate in Info Analytics, Assessment, and User Experience Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Library Services Locations: Binghamton, NY Posted: Aug 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Temporary Ref. No.: 18690 Position ID: 203486 Share About Binghamton University: Binghamton University is a premier public R1 research institution in the State University of New York (SUNY) system that unites more than 130 broadly interdisciplinary educational programs with some of the most vibrant research in the nation. Our unique character - shaped by our mission, outstanding academics, facilities, and community life - promotes extraordinary student success, research, and service; Binghamton University is where our students, faculty and staff thrive. Working at Binghamton University is more than about having a great job - it is about having the opportunity to flourish in an exciting, engaging environment. Our faculty and staff appreciate Binghamton's collegial and inclusive culture and its commitment to excellence, education, innovation and civic engagement. Our diverse campus community contributes to our success. Binghamton merges rigorous academics, distinguished faculty who value cutting-edge, and community-engaged research, teaching and service, exceptional staff, and ultramodern facilities to engage and challenge its 18,000+ students. Our high-achieving student body represents diverse experiences from first-generation college-goers to international students. Beyond their talent, these classmates share a desire to shape the future through technology, insight, intellectual exploration, and community service. We are an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer, and in keeping with this commitment, we welcome all to apply, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Job Description: Budget Title:  Postdoctoral Associate (SL-1) Salary:  $80,000 (full-time, 12-month, temporary) The Binghamton University Libraries invite applications for a two-year Postdoctoral Fellow as the Postdoctoral Associate through SUNY's Promoting Recruitment, Opportunity, Diversity, Inclusion and Growth plus (PRODiG+) program to begin in Fall 2027. The Postdoctoral Associate whose work will advance research and practice in information analytics, organizational assessment, user experience, and evidence-informed decision making. Working at a Carnegie R1 research university, the Associate will explore how information generated through library services, collections, digital environments, and user interactions can be transformed into actionable knowledge that improves organizational performance, enhances user experiences, and demonstrates the impact of research libraries. The PRODiG+ Fellowship is designed with two primary goals: (1) increase the number and share of excellent and diverse faculty committed to advancing the ideals of diversity, equity, and inclusion; and (2) strengthening the pathway for retention and support of these candidates. This Fellowship is for a 12-month appointment for two years (AY27-AY29). The fellow will collaborate with faculty members and receive enhanced support and mentorship by way of career exploration within the Libraries with the goal of developing library career based skills for conversion to a tenure-track senior assistant librarian position upon successful completion of the position as described. More information about the fellowship is available at https://www.suny.edu/prodig-plus/fellowship/ . This position offers a unique opportunity to bridge scholarship and practice. Working collaboratively with library faculty and staff, the Associate will investigate emerging approaches to information analytics, assessment methodologies, user behavior, data visualization, and organizational learning while developing sustainable frameworks and workflows that strengthen library services, inform strategic planning, and support organizational decision making. A key responsibility will be designing scalable methods for collecting, analyzing, visualizing, and communicating organizational data to demonstrate institutional progress and impact. Through this work, the Associate will help further position the Libraries as a leader in evidence-based practice and as an essential partner in the University's research enterprise. The Associate will contribute to the educational mission of the Libraries by designing and leading an undergraduate research internship program focused on information analytics, assessment, user experience, and evidence-informed decision making. The Associate will also establish an undergraduate research internship program that engages students in applied projects focused on information analytics, assessment, and user experience. To support the internship program, the Associate will develop and teach a two-course undergraduate sequence introducing students to assessment methodologies, information behavior, user experience research, information analytics, data visualization, and the communication of evidence for organizational planning and decision making. Both courses will emphasize project-based learning using authentic library datasets and real-world information challenges. The internship program, courses, and applied research agenda are intended to provide a flexible framework. The successful candidate will have considerable latitude to shape these experiences based on their scholarly interests and expertise while advancing the Libraries' strategic priorities and contributing to emerging areas of library and information science Binghamton University Libraries' Glenn G. Bartle Library is home to a newly renovated 35,000 sf third floor which includes a growing Digital Scholarship Center. The facility boasts a state-of-the-art modular classroom as well as attached Data and Recording Studios equipped with specialized and open software. The 3,000 sf MakerLab and complimenting gallery are flanked by private and group study spaces and condensed shelving with over 400,000 browsable physical materials. The open access interdisciplinary laboratory engages students in a way that excites them about future professional practice as creators and analysts through supervised experimentation, research mentorship, and targeted high-impact experiences. Requirements: Be eligible to work in the United States without a visa sponsorship (Note: if you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet the eligibility requirements for this position.) Master's degree from an ALA-accredited library or information science program or an ALA-approved foreign equivalent; Related Doctoral degree from an accredited institution completed prior to start date; Demonstrate personal, academic, and/or work experience engaging with diversity, equity, and inclusion and/or a commitment to facilitating and enhancing diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts in the campus community. Such experience may include, but is not limited to, an academic/scholarly track record focused on diversity, equity, and inclusion; work, volunteer/ unpaid/community service; or related experience/expertise in serving underserved or vulnerable areas and/or populations. Preference will be given to candidates who are: Current SUNY students, alumni, and/or Fellows. From a low-income background (e.g., Pell-eligible as undergraduates), were first-generation college students (students whose parents have not earned a bachelor's degree), have overcome adversity, are AmeriCorps alumni, or are veterans. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated experience conducting quantitative, qualitative, or mixed-methods research. Experience with survey design, usability teaching, ethnographic methods, or other user research techniques. Experience teaching or mentoring undergraduate students. Effective written and oral communication skills, with the ability to convey complex information clearly. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that Binghamton University is not an E-Verify employer. Additional Information: The PRODiG+ Fellowship is open to any and all prospective candidates regardless of race, color, national origin, or sex, and is consistent with all current governing federal and state nondiscrimination laws. All application submissions will be assessed and evaluated in accordance with the required eligibility criteria. Application Instructions: To apply, submit the following materials via Interview Exchange: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover letter Contact information for three professional references In 750 words or less, please provide a response to the following essay prompt: Please describe how you've engaged, facilitated, and/or enhanced diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts in the campus community. Examples could include personal, academic, and/or work experience and may include, but is not limited to, an academic/scholarly track record focused on diversity, equity, and inclusion; work, volunteer/unpaid/ community service; or related experience/ expertise in serving underserved or vulnerable areas and/or populations. Binghamton University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity, and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its services, programs, and activities. To request reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, please contact the ADA Coordinator by completing the Reasonable Accommodation Request Form . The State University of New York is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer.  It is the policy of Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the basis of age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military service member status, marital status, domestic violence victim status, genetic predisposition or carrier status, or arrest and/or criminal conviction record unless based upon a bona fide occupational qualification or other exception. As required by Title IX and its implementing regulations Binghamton University does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the educational programs and activities which it operates.  This requirement extends to employment and admission.  Inquiries about sex discrimination may be directed to the University Title IX Coordinator or directly to the Office of Civil Rights (OCR).  Contact information for the Title IX Coordinator and OCR, as well as the University's complete Non-Discrimination Notice may be found here . Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation.  If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor's Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov. Payroll information can be found on our website https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/payroll/ Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus effective August 1, 2017. Offers of employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a pre-employment background check and verification of degree(s) and credentials. Cover letters may be addressed \"To the Search Committee.\" The position will remain open until filled. For information on the Dual Career Program, please visit: https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/prospective/dual-career/index.html Application Instructions: All applicants must apply via Interview Exchange: http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/candapply.jsp?JOBID=203486 Deadline for Internal Applicants:  August 24, 2026 Deadline for External Applicants:  Open until filled Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the vacancy is filled. Please submit: Resume/Curriculum Vitae, Cover letter, and Contact information for three professional references You may add additional files/documents after uploading your resume. After you fill out your contact information, you will be directed to the upload page. Please login to check/edit your profile or to upload additional documents: http://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/login.jsp . Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Binghamton University State University of New York 4400 Vestal Parkway East, Binghamton, NY 13902"
    },
    "https://binghamton.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203474": {
      "title": "Senior Staff Assistant, External Scholarships and Undergraduate Research Center",
      "description": "Binghamton University\nJob Posting: Senior Staff Assistant, External Scholarships and Undergraduate Research Center Binghamton University \n\tJob Posting: Senior Staff Assistant, External Scholarships and Undergraduate Research Center Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Senior Staff Assistant, External Scholarships and Undergraduate Research Center Category: Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Undergraduate Research & External Scholarships Locations: Binghamton, NY Posted: Aug 7, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 05001 Position ID: 203474 Share About Binghamton University: Binghamton University is a premier public R1 research institution in the State University of New York (SUNY) system that unites more than 130 broadly interdisciplinary educational programs with some of the most vibrant research in the nation. Our unique character - shaped by our mission, outstanding academics, facilities, and community life - promotes extraordinary student success, research, and service; Binghamton University is where our students, faculty and staff thrive. Working at Binghamton University is more than about having a great job - it is about having the opportunity to flourish in an exciting, engaging environment. Our faculty and staff appreciate Binghamton's collegial and inclusive culture and its commitment to excellence, education, innovation and civic engagement. Our diverse campus community contributes to our success. Binghamton merges rigorous academics, distinguished faculty who value cutting-edge, and community-engaged research, teaching and service, exceptional staff, and ultramodern facilities to engage and challenge its 18,000+ students. Our high-achieving student body represents diverse experiences from first-generation college-goers to international students. Beyond their talent, these classmates share a desire to shape the future through technology, insight, intellectual exploration, and community service. We are an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer, and in keeping with this commitment, we welcome all to apply, including veterans and persons with disabilities. Job Description: Budget Title:  Senior Staff Assistant (SL-3) Salary:  $57,151 - $60,000 The External Scholarships and Undergraduate Research Center seeks a Senior Staff Assistant to provide critical operational and programmatic support to the office's undergraduate research program coordination, fellowship and undergraduate research advising, campus outreach, marketing and communications, and Accessibility compliance. The successful candidate will collaborate with campus partners to ensure high-quality service and program delivery for all of ESURC's constituents. The External Scholarships and Undergraduate Research Center develops, recognizes, and awards undergraduate research; promotes and assists students with locating and applying for external scholarships; and provides outreach and advising to undergraduate students, faculty, and the broader campus community. These objectives lay the foundations for providing a transformative learning community that prepares students for advanced education, careers, and purposeful living. The successful candidate will be responsible for: Program Coordination, BUPNUR Summer and Spring programs: Management of faculty recruitment, student recruitment, and student applications for Spring and Summer BUPNUR program cycles Management of BUPNUR student stipends, faculty evaluations, and surveys Manage BUPNUR budget and financial transfers Assist, as needed, with stipend distribution Development of faculty and student stories and outcomes to be shared with external and campus audiences Coordinate management of program's promotional resources and other promotional activities Data management and Assessment of the program's outcomes for grant proposals, donors and reports Represent BUPNUR and Binghamton at undergraduate research conferences and workshops as needed/desired ESURC Office Staff Support: Lead Accessibility compliance Lead office marketing and communications coordination Assist at Summer Orientations and Admitted Student Open Houses Contribute to ESURC office's positive work environment of inclusion and mutual support Maintain professional standards of behavior, appearance, and ethics in the office and when representing the office Provide assistance with strategic planning Maintain contacts with campus offices to support initiatives and working collegially with all constituents and relevant parties within and outside of the university UG Research Advising and Student/Faculty Outreach Provide 4-6 hours/week of scheduled undergraduate research advising each semester Conduct presentations, info sessions, and outreach on behalf of the office as needed UG Research Assessment, Reporting, Marketing Contribute to ESURC Weave Reporting and a new Annual Undergraduate Research Report Contribute to new story-telling initiatives around UG research and creative activity Awards Selection Coordination Provide coordination for Chancellor's, President's, and Provost's Awards nomination processes and selection committees Coordinate President's Awards Luncheon Serve on evaluation committee for URA and UCPF awards Requirements: Bachelor's degree 2+ years experience in higher education administrative offices Demonstrated competency working in Google, Microsoft, Canva, and Adobe software suites Demonstrated commitment to and technical proficiency in meeting accessibility standards Ability to effectively, professionally, and tactfully interact and communicate, both orally and in writing, with a diverse community of students, faculty, staff, and the public Effective organization skills and attention to detail Preferred: Experience in an Academic Affairs administrative office Experience with undergraduate research (personal or professional) Familiarity with national fellowships and scholarships Experience with records and database management Experience with student advising Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. If you currently need sponsorship or will need it in the future to maintain employment authorization, you do not meet eligibility requirements. Additionally, please note that Binghamton University is not an E-Verify employer. Additional Information: Offers of employment will be contingent upon successful completion of a pre-employment background check and verification of degree(s) and credentials Binghamton University is a tobacco-free campus. Pursuant to Executive Order 161, no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation.  If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Governor's Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov Payroll information can be found on our website https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/payroll/ Cover letters may be addressed \"To the Search Committee.\" Postings active on the website, accept applications until closure. For information on the Dual Career Program, please visit: https://www.binghamton.edu/offices/human-resources/prospective/dual-career/index.html Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer The State University of New York is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer.  It is the policy of Binghamton University to provide for and promote equal opportunity employment, compensation, and other terms and conditions of employment without discrimination on the basis of age, race, color, religion, disability, national origin, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, veteran or military servic